Description: Stereo Demonstrator: 3D models in stereo, with a 3D cursor
 The Stereo Demonstrator, by KDAB, shows 3D models (OBJ, FBX, glTF)
 on stereo displays with a 3D cursor drawn where the mouse meets the
 model, automatic focus over a focus area, asymmetric frusta, an eye
 separation taken from the focus distance, pop-out and the field of
 view from the screen's physical size.
 .
 This is the stereo version by Sparky Stereo OS. The 3D area is the
 one stereo surface: a quad-buffer OpenGL context where the stack
 gives one, or the two eyes drawn side by side and declared to the
 desktop, which makes every screen's format from them (3D televisions,
 anaglyph on any monitor, interleaved and frame-sequential displays,
 two-output pairs, headsets). The side menu stays an ordinary 2D
 surface. The program's 3D options are Enable 3D, the stereo output
 path, the render resolution per eye and a shortcut to the display
 settings; the demonstrator's own controls stay under Advanced.
